    "title": "Live Blog: Tottenham vs Atlético Madrid LIVE score and updates in the Champions League",
    "text": "Atlético Madrid loses 3-2 but advances to the Quarterfinals with a 7-5 aggregate score.90+1 Simons scores from a penalty in stoppage time, and Tottenham wins the match.David Hancko scores the equalizer, bringing a sense of calm to Simeone.52'. Simons breathes new life into Tottenham, who now lead the match.47'. Pressure from Cholo's side; they win back possession, and Lookman sets up Julián Álvarez.The second half is now underway in London—45 more minutes of Champions League action.Cholo's team had the best chances of the first half, including attempts by Giuliano Simeone and Julian Álvarez.30' Kolo Muani capitalizes on lax marking to make it 1-0 for Tottenham against Atlético. Aggregate: 5-3 to Cholo's men.Lookman finishes, but the referee disallows it for offside.Tottenham seeks a miracle against Atlético Madrid in the Champions League.Tottenham Hotspur host Atlético Madrid in the UEFA Champions League Round of 16 second leg.Spurs are going through a major crisis, which not even the arrival of Igor Tudor has been able to fix, and they need a miracle to stay alive in the competition.On paper, Diego Simeone’s side are favorites to advance, although the Champions League can always deliver surprises.Despite playing at home, Tottenham arrive in poor form. They are just one point above the relegation zone in the Premier League and suffered a 5-2 defeat at the Wanda Metropolitano in the first leg.The English side must win by at least three goals to force extra time. Any other result, even a win by one or two goals, will eliminate them.Atlético Madrid, meanwhile, have little chance in LaLiga title race, but can build momentum through this competition and upcoming matches.Simeone’s team can lose by up to two goals and still secure their place in the quarter-finals.The winner of this tie will face either Barcelona or Newcastle United in the quarter-finals.The matches are scheduled for April 7–8 (first leg) and April 14–15 (second leg).Possible lineups for Tottenham vs Atlético Madrid Tottenham: Guglielmo Vicario; Pedro Porro, Kevin Danso, Romero, Micky van de Ven; Archie Gray, Pape Matar Sarr, Mathys Tel, Gallagher; Randal Kolo Muani, Dominic Solanke. Atlético de Madrid: Juan Musso; Marc Pubill, Robin Le Normand, Dávid Hancko, Matteo Ruggeri; Giuliano Simeone, Marcos Llorente, Johnny Cardoso, Ademola Lookman; Antoine Griezmann, Julián Álvarez. Watch beIN SPORTS Xtra live for free on YouTube",
